										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<section class="ga-title stacking-slide dark-blue-section-background-color container-fluid internaltitle-block">
			<div class="internal-title alignwide internalpage container">

				<div class="internal-title-wrapper">

					<div id="internal-title-header" class="internal-title-header medium">
						Demonstration Alert – U.S. Embassy Libya  (September 11, 2026) 
					</div>

						
				</div>

			</div>

		</section>

<section  class="ga-content-block stacking-slide white-section-background-color paragraphsection">
	<div class="paragraph alignwide container meta-info-top">

		
	</div>

	<div class="paragraph alignwide container">

		<div class="row">

			
				<p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Tripoli, Libya</p>
<p><strong>Event: </strong>The U.S. Embassy strongly encourages U.S. citizens to stay away from sites of recent protests, maintain a high level of vigilance and practice good situational awareness. Press and social media reported protests in Tripoli over the past week targeting international organization and government buildings. Additional protests may occur with little notice.</p>
<p>Currently we are not aware of specific, credible threats against U.S. citizens in Libya, but U.S. citizens should review the current Department of State <a href="https://travel.state.gov/en/international-travel/travel-advisories/libya.html">Level 4 Travel Advisory for Libya</a>. U.S. citizens who choose to remain in Libya should prepare contingency plans for emergency situations.</p>
<p><strong>Actions to take: </strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Avoid areas of recent protests.</li>
<li>Monitor local media for updates.</li>
<li>Be aware of your surroundings.</li>
<li>Keep a low profile.</li>
<li>Have evacuation plans that do not rely on U.S. Government assistance.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Assistance</strong>:  U.S. citizens in Libya who need emergency assistance should contact the U.S Embassy in Tunis at <a href="mailto:TunisACS@state.gov">TunisACS@state.gov</a> or +216 71 107 000. The after-hours emergency number for U.S. citizens in Libya is +216 29 980 978 (also works with WhatsApp).</p>
<p>Department of State – Consular Affairs: 888-407-4747 or 202-501-4444</p>
<p><a href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/libya-travel-advisory.html">Libya Travel Advisory  </a></p>
<p>Enroll in <a href="https://step.state.gov/step/">Smart Traveler Enrollment Program (STEP) </a> to receive security updates.</p>
<p>Find us on <a href="https://twitter.com/USEmbassyLibya">Twitter</a>, <a href="https://www.facebook.com/USEmbassyLibya">Facebook </a>, and <a href="https://www.instagram.com/USEmbassyLibya/">Instagram </a> using the tag: @USEmbassyLibya</p>
</p>

				
		</div>

	</div>

</section>
